  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 30,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that we have nuclear weapons and nuclear power plants you might think that it was always"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4690,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Inevitable that we would be able to harness the energy inside the nucleus of atoms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9010,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that was far from the case in fact serious scientists, thought the idea was laughable like Nobel laureate Robert"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16170,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Millikan who in 1928 said there is no likelihood man can ever tap the power of the atom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21460,
    "dDurationMs": 5569,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The glib supposition of utilizing atomic energy when our coal has run out is a completely unscientific"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27550,
    "dDurationMs": 7759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Utopian dream or as Rutherford put it anyone who expects a source of power from the transformation of these atoms is talking moonshine"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35559,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now there was good reason for their pessimism when Becquerel first observed to radioactivity he thought it was a phenomenon similar to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43480,
    "dDurationMs": 570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "phosphorescence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44050,
    "dDurationMs": 3079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's when you shine radiation like light onto an object"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47129,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it absorbs that energy and later"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49840,
    "dDurationMs": 7039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Reradiates it in a different part of the spectrum now uranium ore was known to do this as I witnessed firsthand. Oh, yeah"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57520,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "X yes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59260,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fluorescent uranium ore"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63340,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64720,
    "dDurationMs": 4339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here, it's absorbing UV light and reradiating it as visible light in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69880,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1896 Becquerel performed experiments where he placed uranium ore in the sunshine on top of some wrapped up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75820,
    "dDurationMs": 2839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Photographic film he found that the film was exposed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78909,
    "dDurationMs": 5450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Seemingly by invisible rays from the uranium ore that penetrated the paper when the uranium was excited by the sunlight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84670,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But one day when he went to do his experiment the weather in Paris was lousy so he put the uranium and the photographic film"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91180,
    "dDurationMs": 4759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Inside a drawer and a few days later even though the uranium hadn't seen the Sun"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95939,
    "dDurationMs": 1801,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He decided to develop the film anyway"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97740,
    "dDurationMs": 5459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what he found was that the photographic film had been exposed just as before"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103659,
    "dDurationMs": 3110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even though the uranium was not excited by sunlight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106869,
    "dDurationMs": 6740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this was not a phosphorescence phenomenon some type of radiation and therefore energy was coming out of a rock"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114250,
    "dDurationMs": 1409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unprovoked"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115659,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how could a seemingly inert object like a rock give off energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120280,
    "dDurationMs": 6229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where is it getting that energy from it was a mystery that seemed to violate the law of conservation of energy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126790,
    "dDurationMs": 3499,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is until Einstein published his famous e equals mc-squared"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130660,
    "dDurationMs": 2209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which suggested a source of energy for the?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133260,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Might be the mass of the nucleus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135629,
    "dDurationMs": 7070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just a tiny bit of mass can give you a lot of energy and this premise was enough for science fiction writers to let their"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142950,
    "dDurationMs": 5990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imaginations run wild like HG Wells who in 1914 published the book the world set free"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149310,
    "dDurationMs": 7819,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which includes the first mention of the words atomic bomb he envisioned a uranium based hand grenade that would continue to explode"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157799,
    "dDurationMs": 7640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "indefinitely but to scientists this was completely detached from reality as Einstein in 1933 put it there is not the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165510,
    "dDurationMs": 7009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "slightest indication that nuclear energy will ever be obtainable it would mean that the atom would have to be shattered at will and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172680,
    "dDurationMs": 3949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's just the thing people had no ability to make a nucleus do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176760,
    "dDurationMs": 5389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anything all we were observing was the natural process of radioactive decay atoms of a particular"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182579,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unstable isotope decaying at random with some characteristic half-life"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187079,
    "dDurationMs": 6650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the energy given off although immense on the scale of an atom is pretty insignificant on the scale of people and the world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193890,
    "dDurationMs": 2330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the fission of a single uranium atom releases"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196620,
    "dDurationMs": 5929,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Twenty times less energy than the amount required to raise a grain of sand the thickness of a piece of paper"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203069,
    "dDurationMs": 7460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now up until 1932 the only known particle in the nucleus was the proton so if you wanted to alter a nucleus you could conceivably"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210780,
    "dDurationMs": 1549,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fire a proton at it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212329,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But since the nucleus and the proton are both positively charged they repel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216599,
    "dDurationMs": 6050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you'd have to fire the proton in with such high speed and accuracy to get it to hit and stick to a target and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222780,
    "dDurationMs": 2929,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even then if you're successful you've only affected one nucleus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225709,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which at best can't even lift a grain of sand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228690,
    "dDurationMs": 4429,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can see why the Nobel Prize winners were saying nuclear weapons not gonna happen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233639,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then comes the discovery of the neutron and the neutron changes everything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238530,
    "dDurationMs": 3229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because as an uncharged nuclear particle it can drift"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242489,
    "dDurationMs": 2929,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ghostly undeflected through matter until it hits a nucleus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246120,
    "dDurationMs": 5059,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Transforming it into something else and this leads to the Epiphany of a man named Leo Szilard"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251359,
    "dDurationMs": 6630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now's a lard read the world set free, so he's already imagined a future in which nuclear energy is harnessed by weaponry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257989,
    "dDurationMs": 5369,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And he remembers the exact moment he comes up with this idea as he's crossing the street in London"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263700,
    "dDurationMs": 7459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He says it suddenly occurred to me that if we could find an element which is split by neutrons and which would emit two neutrons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271160,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when it absorbed one Neutron then such an element"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273770,
    "dDurationMs": 4139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If assembled in sufficiently large mass could sustain a nuclear chain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278250,
    "dDurationMs": 720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reaction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278970,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words the neutron"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280620,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Enables us to trigger"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281940,
    "dDurationMs": 7130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nuclear reactions at will and if there's a nucleus which when it splits in this way releases two neutrons it could trigger more and more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289070,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fission's and an exponentially increasing rate the nucleus that has this property is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295020,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "uranium-235"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296060,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact on average it releases two and a half neutrons every time it divides"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300060,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now all of a sudden you have the possibility of splitting zillions of nuclei"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305790,
    "dDurationMs": 3559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simultaneously releasing incredible amounts of energy all at once"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309680,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's an atomic bomb now if you want more control over this release of energy as in a nuclear power plant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315150,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315650,
    "dDurationMs": 3899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then you have to absorb a few neutrons so that the fission of one nucleus only"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319710,
    "dDurationMs": 2899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Causes the fission of one other nucleus on average"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322620,
    "dDurationMs": 6410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then you have a steady chain reaction that emits the same amount of energy each instant the challenge is that this is like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329340,
    "dDurationMs": 7190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Balancing on a knife-edge absorb too many neutrons and the chain reaction quickly decays to nothing absorb too few and the rate of reactions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336690,
    "dDurationMs": 7339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Increases exponentially and soon you're back to a bomb or Chernobyl so if not for the existence of the neutron a neutral"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344250,
    "dDurationMs": 6529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nuclear particle to trigger reactions that occurs in greater numbers relative to protons in the larger nuclei meaning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350780,
    "dDurationMs": 5910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're likely to be given off when a large nucleus splits well, then maybe as many brilliant scientists suspected"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356690,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It would be impossible to harness the energy in the nucleus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359670,
    "dDurationMs": 6589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as it is in our universe the neutron is the hero or the villain of nuclear physics"
    } ]
  }, {
